# OCULUM — Development north star

Keep this in mind for **all** OCULUM work (rules, code, art, UX, balance)—not only when adding cards.

## The goal

Build toward an **epic, deep CCG** with lasting identity—not a shallow prototype that piles on content.

Tagline fantasy: *Things only fully exist when Witnessed.*

## Never lose the core

- Loop: **Play Veiled → spend Sight to Witness → Gaze / Graft / Rite / Stance → Pass → Resolve altitudes**
- Resources: **Essence** (play) · **Sight** (Witness / Gaze)
- Board: **High / Mid / Low** with distinct incentives
- Wins: **Break** (Will) · **Eclipse** · **Law / turns**
- Schools are heresies of one Eye faith—expand them, don’t blur them into generic fantasy

## Quality bar every change

- Prefer depth and clarity over feature spam
- New systems must combo with the existing set, not ignore it
- Printed text, Codex, art, and `match.ts` behavior stay aligned (see card-design rule)
- Feel-pass UX (Law, Gaze, Stance, enemy turns, Resolve) stays honest and readable
- Art: original subjects in OCULUM style; never copy reference sheets

## When unsure

Ask: *Does this make Witnessing matter more, decks more interesting, or the world more itself?* If no, cut or rethink.
